  "passage": "Last Saturday, our school hosted its annual Spring Fair in the main hall and playground. The event aimed to raise money for a local charity, and it was definitely a big success, raising over £500 with over 200 people attending. One of the most popular stalls was selling delicious homemade chocolate biscuits and cakes. Many visitors said these treats were the best part of the day. Another attraction was a craft table where children could decorate candles with stickers and paint. This was very popular, and some kids even made multiple candles to take home. Additionally, a local farm brought in several gentle rabbits for a petting session, which was loved by younger children, though one parent made a complaint about the noise level. To improve future events, the organisers sold tickets online before the fair, which helped reduce waiting times. They also plan to multiply the number of volunteers next year to handle the crowd better. Overall, the Spring Fair was a wonderful community event that brought everyone together.",
